    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm358_purpose">Dual op-amp for single-supply use</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm358_description">Two op-amps in one package. The input range includes ground and the output swings close to it, so it works from a single supply.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm324_purpose">Quad op-amp for single-supply use</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm324_description">Four op-amps of the same design as the LM358. The input range includes ground, so it works from a single supply.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_tl072_purpose">Dual low-noise JFET-input op-amp</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_tl072_description">Two op-amps with JFET inputs, giving very low input bias current, low noise and a higher slew rate than the LM358. Usually run from a split supply.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_op07_purpose">Precision op-amp with very low offset</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_op07_description">A single bipolar op-amp with very low input offset voltage and drift. The offset can be trimmed with a potentiometer on the NULL pins. Used for precise DC amplification.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm393_purpose">Dual comparator, open-collector outputs</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm393_description">Two voltage comparators. The open-collector outputs need a pull-up resistor and can pull up to a voltage other than the supply.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm339_purpose">Quad comparator, open-collector outputs</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm339_description">Four comparators of the same design as the LM393. The open-collector outputs need a pull-up resistor.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_ne555_purpose">Timer for delays and oscillators</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_ne555_description">A bipolar timer that makes a single delay (monostable) or a square wave (astable), timed by an external resistor and capacitor. The output can source and sink a large current.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n3904_purpose">General-purpose NPN small-signal transistor</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n3904_description">For small loads, logic-level switching and amplifiers. The complement of the 2N3906.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n3906_purpose">General-purpose PNP small-signal transistor</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n3906_description">The PNP complement of the 2N3904, for the same kind of small-signal work.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_pn2222a_purpose">NPN transistor for switching and amplifying</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_pn2222a_description">Handles more collector current than the 2N3904. The PN2222A is the TO-92 version of the metal-can 2N2222A.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_pn2907a_purpose">PNP transistor for switching and amplifying</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_pn2907a_description">The PNP complement of the PN2222A, and the TO-92 version of the metal-can 2N2907A.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bc548_purpose">General-purpose NPN amplifier transistor</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bc548_description">A European general-purpose NPN, sold in gain groups A, B and C. Its TO-92 pin order differs from the 2N3904.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bd139_purpose">NPN medium-power transistor</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bd139_description">For currents in the ampere range, in a TO-126 (TO-225) package that mounts on a heatsink. The complement of the BD140.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bd140_purpose">PNP medium-power transistor</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bd140_description">The PNP complement of the BD139, in the same package.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n7000_purpose">N-channel small-signal MOSFET</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n7000_description">A small N-channel enhancement MOSFET in TO-92 for switching small loads from logic outputs.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n7002_purpose">N-channel small-signal MOSFET, SOT-23</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_2n7002_description">The surface-mount counterpart of the 2N7000, often used as a level shifter or a small load switch.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n4148_purpose">Fast-switching small-signal diode</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n4148_description">A small, fast silicon diode for signal paths, clamping and logic. Not meant for power rectification.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n914_purpose">Fast-switching small-signal diode</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n914_description">An older type with ratings close to the 1N4148; the two are used interchangeably.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n4001_1n4007_purpose">General-purpose rectifier diodes</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n4001_1n4007_description">Silicon rectifiers for mains and power-supply rectification. The members differ only in maximum reverse voltage.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n5817_purpose">Schottky rectifier with low forward voltage</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n5817_description">For low-voltage power supplies and reverse-polarity protection. Its reverse leakage is higher than that of a silicon diode.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n5819_purpose">Schottky rectifier, highest voltage of its series</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_1n5819_description">From the same series as the 1N5817, with a higher reverse voltage rating and a higher forward voltage.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bat54_purpose">Small-signal Schottky diode, SOT-23</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_bat54_description">A low-current Schottky diode for signal clamping and low-drop OR-ing. Dual versions with other pinouts are sold under related names.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_sd103_purpose">Small-signal Schottky diode, axial</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_sd103_description">An axial small-signal Schottky diode, sold in A, B and C voltage grades.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_78xx_purpose">Fixed positive linear regulators</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_78xx_description">Three-terminal positive regulators; the last two digits give the output voltage. They have built-in current limiting and thermal shutdown.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_79xx_purpose">Fixed negative linear regulators</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_79xx_description">The negative counterparts of the 78xx. Their pin order differs from the 78xx.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm317_purpose">Adjustable positive linear regulator</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm317_description">A three-terminal adjustable regulator: two resistors set the output from the reference voltage between OUT and ADJ.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm337_purpose">Adjustable negative linear regulator</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm337_description">The negative counterpart of the LM317, adjusted the same way with two resistors. Its pin order differs from the LM317.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_tl431_purpose">Adjustable shunt voltage reference</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_tl431_description">A programmable shunt reference: two resistors set the cathode voltage anywhere from the reference voltage up to its maximum. Common in power-supply feedback loops with an optocoupler.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_74hc_purpose">High-speed CMOS logic family</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_74hc_description">A CMOS logic family; inputs need CMOS levels (for TTL-level inputs there is 74HCT). The members listed are common gates, a flip-flop and a shift register. Values are from the 74HC00.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm35_purpose">Analog temperature sensor, output in °C</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_lm35_description">The output voltage is proportional to the temperature in Celsius, with no calibration needed. Readings below zero need a negative supply or an offset circuit.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_tmp36_purpose">Low-voltage analog temperature sensor</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_tmp36_description">The output has an offset, so it reads temperatures below zero from a single low-voltage supply.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_mc34063_purpose">DC-DC converter controller with built-in switch</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_mc34063_description">Contains an oscillator, a comparator and a switch transistor for step-down, step-up and inverting converters with few external parts.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_uc384x_purpose">Current-mode PWM controllers</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_uc384x_description">PWM controllers for flyback and forward converters. The members differ in start and stop thresholds and in maximum duty cycle.</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_icl7660_purpose">Charge-pump voltage inverter</string>
    <string name="jellybean_parts_icl7660_description">Makes a negative voltage from a positive supply with two capacitors and no inductor. It can also double a voltage.</string>
</resources>
